ct Folder:** Inspect the active workspace root, switch folders, or trigger a disk rescan."},"20":{"id":"/docs/configuration-18","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#3-compiler--preview","content":"**Typst Compiler Version:** Use built-in `0.15.1` or download/activate legacy `0.14.2`, `0.13.1`, or `0.12.0` releases."},"21":{"id":"/docs/configuration-19","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#3-compiler--preview","content":"**Auto-Compile on Type:** Incrementally recompile while editing (enabled by default)."},"22":{"id":"/docs/configuration-20","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#3-compiler--preview","content":"**Typing Debounce Interval:** Configurable from `50 ms` to `800 ms` (default `120 ms`)."},"23":{"id":"/docs/configuration-21","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#3-compiler--preview","content":"**Preview Rasterization Scale:** `1.5x Fast`, `2.0x Crisp` (default), or `3.0x Ultra HiDPI`."},"24":{"id":"/docs/configuration-22","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#3-compiler--preview","content":"**Preview Interaction:** Toggle **Auto-Jump** source selection sync and **Hand Pan** mode."},"25":{"id":"/docs/configuration-23","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#4-spell--grammar","content":"**Enable Spell & Grammar Checking:** Master toggle (disabled by default)."},"26":{"id":"/docs/configuration-24","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#4-spell--grammar","content":"**Auto-Check While Typing:** Debounced background checking (`150 ms`–`2000 ms`, default `450 ms`)."},"27":{"id":"/docs/configuration-25","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#4-spell--grammar","content":"**Grammar & Typography Rules:** Toggle `nlprule` and pure-Rust typography/repetition checks."},"28":{"id":"/docs/configuration-26","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#4-spell--grammar","content":"**Document Language Override:** `Auto` (reads `#set text(lang: ...)` or runs Lingua detection) or explicit `en` / `de` / `fr` / `es`."},"29":{"id":"/docs/configuration-27","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#4-spell--grammar","content":"**Dictionaries:** Download/remove Tier-1 language packs, import Tier-2 `.dic`/`.aff` files, and manage ignored words."},"30":{"id":"/docs/configuration-28","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"On macOS, `Ctrl` corresponds to `Cmd` (`Modifiers::COMMAND` in `app/src/platform/shortcuts.rs`):"},"31":{"id":"/docs/configuration-29","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| New File in Project | `Ctrl + N`      | `Cmd + N` |","table":"table-0"},"32":{"id":"/docs/configuration-30","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Open Project Folder | `Ctrl + O`      | `Cmd + O` |","table":"table-0"},"33":{"id":"/docs/configuration-31","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action           | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Save Active File | `Ctrl + S`      | `Cmd + S` |","table":"table-0"},"34":{"id":"/docs/configuration-32","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action     | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ---------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Export PDF | `Ctrl + E`      | `Cmd + E` |","table":"table-0"},"35":{"id":"/docs/configuration-33","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action        | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Open Settings | `Ctrl + ,`      | `Cmd + ,` |","table":"table-0"},"36":{"id":"/docs/configuration-34","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Toggle Left Sidebar | `Ctrl + B`      | `Cmd + B` |","table":"table-0"},"37":{"id":"/docs/configuration-35","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Toggle Bottom Panel | `Ctrl + J`      | `Cmd + J` |","table":"table-0"},"38":{"id":"/docs/configuration-36","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action                | Windows / Linux | macOS |\n| --------------------- | --------------- | ----- |\n| Rescan Folder on Disk | `F5`            | `F5`  |","table":"table-0"},"39":{"id":"/docs/configuration-37","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action                          | Windows / Linux                               | macOS                         |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Undo / Redo (incl. CRDT Collab) | `Ctrl + Z` / `Ctrl + Y` or `Ctrl + Shift + Z` | `Cmd + Z` / `Cmd + Shift + Z` |","table":"table-0"},"40":{"id":"/docs/configuration-38","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action                          | Windows / Linux              | macOS                       |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Cut / Copy / Paste / Select All | `Ctrl + X` / `C` / `V` / `A` | `Cmd + X` / `C` / `V` / `A` |","table":"table-0"},"41":{"id":"/docs/configuration-39","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Action              | Windows / Linux      | macOS               |\n| ------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Zoom Preview Canvas | `Ctrl + Mouse Wheel` | `Cmd + Mouse Wheel` |","table":"table-0"},"42":{"id":"/docs/configuration-40","page_id":"/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration#localization","content":"UI strings live in monolingual Weblate-compatible YAML files under `locales/` (`locales/en.yml`, `locales/de.yml`) powered by `rust-i18n`. New translations can be added by creating a matching `locales/<lang>.yml` file and registering it in `app/src/core/i18n.rs`."},"43":{"id":"/docs/contributing","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/contributing"},"44":{"id":"/docs/contributing-0","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing","content":"Build, test, lint, and contribute to the azo-type desktop app (/app) and documentation website (/website)."},"45":{"id":"/docs/contributing-1","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/contributing#repository-structure","content":"Repository Structure"},"46":{"id":"/docs/contributing-2","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"Working on the Desktop App (`/app`)"},"47":{"id":"/docs/contributing-3","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/contributing#key-architectural-rules","content":"Key Architectural Rules"},"48":{"id":"/docs/contributing-4","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-website-website","content":"Working on the Website (`/website`)"},"49":{"id":"/docs/contributing-5","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing","content":"Contributions to **azo-type** are welcome across both the Rust desktop IDE (`/app`) and this documentation site (`/website`). All code in this repository is licensed under the **GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)**."},"50":{"id":"/docs/contributing-6","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"Before submitting any pull request touching Rust code, run the unified quality gate from the repository root:"},"51":{"id":"/docs/contributing-7","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"`./scripts/check.sh` enforces four checks:"},"52":{"id":"/docs/contributing-8","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"`cargo fmt --check --manifest-path app/Cargo.toml`"},"53":{"id":"/docs/contributing-9","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"`cargo clippy --all-targets --manifest-path app/Cargo.toml -- -D warnings`"},"54":{"id":"/docs/contributing-10","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"`python3 scripts/verify_structural_rules.py` (enforces inward layer boundaries, `//!` module docs, file size limits, externalized tests in `app/src/tests/`, and `docs/agent/PROJECT_MAP.md` synchronization)"},"55":{"id":"/docs/contributing-11","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"`cargo test --manifest-path app/Cargo.toml` (unit tests, integration tests, and headless `egui_kittest` UI tests)"},"56":{"id":"/docs/contributing-12","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-desktop-app-app","content":"To inspect line coverage with `cargo-llvm-cov`:"},"57":{"id":"/docs/contributing-13","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#key-architectural-rules","content":"`app/src/core/` must remain pure Rust with **zero** GUI (`egui`/`eframe`), OS dialog (`rfd`/`muda`), or async/P2P (`tokio`/`iroh`) imports."},"58":{"id":"/docs/contributing-14","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#key-architectural-rules","content":"Do not place inline `mod tests { ... }` blocks inside production `.rs` files—wire unit tests via `#[cfg(test)] #[path = \"...\"] mod tests;` into `app/src/tests/`."},"59":{"id":"/docs/contributing-15","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#key-architectural-rules","content":"Create commits on a dedicated branch using Conventional Commits (`feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `docs(...)`, `refactor(...)`, `test(...)`)."},"60":{"id":"/docs/contributing-16","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-website-website","content":"The marketing pages and documentation are built with Next.js static export (`output: 'export'`) and Fumadocs."},"61":{"id":"/docs/contributing-17","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#working-on-the-website-website","content":"Documentation pages live in `website/content/docs/*.mdx`, ordered by `website/content/docs/meta.json`."},"62":{"id":"/docs/features","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"page","content":"Features","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features"},"63":{"id":"/docs/features-0","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features","content":"Deep dive into azo-type capabilities—live preview, Typst version switching, AST outline, P2P collaboration, PDF/A export, and offline proofreading."},"64":{"id":"/docs/features-1","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features#live-preview--interactive-source-sync","content":"Live Preview & Interactive Source Sync"},"65":{"id":"/docs/features-2","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features#multi-version-typst-compiler-engine","content":"Multi-Version Typst Compiler Engine"},"66":{"id":"/docs/features-3","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features#hierarchical-ast-document-outline","content":"Hierarchical AST Document Outline"},"67":{"id":"/docs/features-4","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"Zero-Server P2P Collaboration"},"68":{"id":"/docs/features-5","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features#standards-compliant-pdf-export","content":"Standards-Compliant PDF Export"},"69":{"id":"/docs/features-6","page_id":"/docs/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features#offline-spell--grammar-checking","content":"Offline Spell & Grammar Checking"},"70":{"id":"/docs/features-7","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#live-preview--interactive-source-sync","content":"`azo-type` renders compiled Typst pages to RGBA textures using `typst_render` on a non-blocking worker thread:"},"71":{"id":"/docs/features-8","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#live-preview--interactive-source-sync","content":"**Rasterization DPI:** Choose between **1.5x Fast**, **2.0x Crisp** (default), and **3.0x Ultra HiDPI** in Settings."},"72":{"id":"/docs/features-9","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#live-preview--interactive-source-sync","content":"**Zoom & Navigation:** Toggle **Fit Width**, select preset zoom percentages (`50%`–`200%`), or hold `Ctrl` + mouse wheel over the preview (`25%`–`400%`)."},"73":{"id":"/docs/features-10","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#live-preview--interactive-source-sync","content":"**Click & Drag Text Selection:** Select text directly on rendered preview pages to copy it or automatically jump the editor cursor back to the corresponding Typst source range (**Auto-Jump**)."},"74":{"id":"/docs/features-11","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#live-preview--interactive-source-sync","content":"**Hand Pan Mode:** Switch to **Hand Pan** in the preview toolbar to drag-pan across zoomed pages without triggering text selection."},"75":{"id":"/docs/features-12","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#multi-version-typst-compiler-engine","content":"While Typst `0.15.1` is compiled directly into `azo-type`, older documents may target earlier Typst releases. In **Settings → Compiler & Preview** (or by clicking the Typst version badge in the status bar), you can switch between:"},"76":{"id":"/docs/features-13","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#multi-version-typst-compiler-engine","content":"**Typst `0.15.1`** (built-in offline default)"},"77":{"id":"/docs/features-14","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#multi-version-typst-compiler-engine","content":"**Legacy Typst `0.14.2`, `0.13.1`, and `0.12.0`** (downloaded on demand from official Typst GitHub releases for your host triple and verified against embedded SHA-256 checksums before activation)"},"78":{"id":"/docs/features-15","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#hierarchical-ast-document-outline","content":"The outline parser (`app/src/core/outline.rs`) inspects the Typst AST (`typst-syntax`) rather than naive regexes:"},"79":{"id":"/docs/features-16","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#hierarchical-ast-document-outline","content":"Extracts `= ...` markup headings and `#heading(level: ...)[...]` calls while ignoring headings inside comments, raw code blocks, and `show heading.where(...)` styling rules."},"80":{"id":"/docs/features-17","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#hierarchical-ast-document-outline","content":"Recursively resolves `#include \"...\"` and `#module` imports across project files and merges compiled outline items from templates."},"81":{"id":"/docs/features-18","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#hierarchical-ast-document-outline","content":"Also parses Markdown `# Heading` sections and BibTeX `@article{key, ...}` citation entries."},"82":{"id":"/docs/features-19","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#hierarchical-ast-document-outline","content":"Assigns hierarchical numbering (`1`, `1.1`, `1.1.1`) and highlights the heading matching your current cursor position."},"83":{"id":"/docs/features-20","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"Open **Project → Collaboration (P2P)...** to co-author an entire project folder in real time without central servers:"},"84":{"id":"/docs/features-21","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"**CRDT Synchronization (`yrs`):** Multi-file project state is synced via Yjs CRDT updates (`Origin::from(\"local\")` vs `Origin::from(\"remote\")`), preserving cursor positions with `StickyIndex` and isolating each peer's undo/redo history (`yrs::UndoManager`)."},"85":{"id":"/docs/features-22","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"**Direct QUIC Transport (`iroh`):** Hosts bind an `iroh` QUIC endpoint (`b\"azo-type/collab/v1\"`) and generate a 256-bit secret invite ticket prefixed with `typst-collab-v1:`."},"86":{"id":"/docs/features-23","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"**LAN / Localhost Only Mode:** Optionally disable public relays when collaborating on a trusted local network."},"87":{"id":"/docs/features-24","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"**Peer Presence & Persistence:** Displays connected peers with custom display names, cursor colors, active file indicators, and connection routes (`Direct` vs `Relay` with RTT). Snapshots are saved to `.typst-collab/` with path-traversal protection and deterministic conflict naming (`<stem>.conflict-<id>.<ext>`)."},"88":{"id":"/docs/features-25","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#zero-server-p2p-collaboration","content":"Treat `typst-collab-v1:` invite tickets like passwords—anyone holding a ticket can join the active P2P session. Use the **Mask Ticket** toggle when screen-sharing."},"89":{"id":"/docs/features-26","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#standards-compliant-pdf-export","content":"Press `Ctrl+E` (`Cmd+E` on macOS) or choose **File → Export PDF...** to configure standards-checked PDF output:"},"90":{"id":"/docs/features-27","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#standards-compliant-pdf-export","content":"**PDF Versions:** `1.4`, `1.5`, `1.6`, `1.7` (default), and `2.0`."},"91":{"id":"/docs/features-28","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#standards-compliant-pdf-export","content":"**PDF/A Archival Standards (ISO 19005):** `PDF/A-1b`, `PDF/A-1a`, `PDF/A-2b`, `PDF/A-2u`, `PDF/A-2a`, `PDF/A-3b`, `PDF/A-3u`, `PDF/A-3a`, `PDF/A-4`, `PDF/A-4f`, and `PDF/A-4e`."},"92":{"id":"/docs/features-29","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#standards-compliant-pdf-export","content":"**Accessibility:** Toggle **PDF/UA-1** (ISO 14289-1) and **Tagged PDF** structure tree generation."},"93":{"id":"/docs/features-30","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#standards-compliant-pdf-export","content":"**Compatibility Guard:** Automatically validates combinations (for example, `PDF/A-1` requires `PDF 1.4` and `PDF/A-4` requires `PDF 2.0`), offers a one-click compatible version switch, and displays the equivalent `typst compile --pdf-standard` CLI flags."},"94":{"id":"/docs/features-31","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#offline-spell--grammar-checking","content":"Disabled by default so it stays out of your way until needed, offline proofreading runs strictly locally inside **azo-type**:"},"95":{"id":"/docs/features-32","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#offline-spell--grammar-checking","content":"**Typst-Aware Prose Extraction:** Masks code, math, labels, comments, and syntax tokens before checking prose."},"96":{"id":"/docs/features-33","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#offline-spell--grammar-checking","content":"**Tier-1 Language Packs (`en`, `de`, `fr`, `es`):** Download Hunspell dictionaries (`spellbook`) and `nlprule` grammar binaries on demand with SHA-256 verification. Language detection (`lingua`) or `#set text(lang: \"...\")` automatically selects the active language when set to `Auto`."},"97":{"id":"/docs/features-34","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#offline-spell--grammar-checking","content":"**Tier-2 Custom Hunspell Dictionaries:** Import any local `.dic` / `.aff` dictionary pair from disk (automatically transcoded to UTF-8)."},"98":{"id":"/docs/features-35","page_id":"/docs/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features#offline-spell--grammar-checking","content":"**Interactive Diagnostics:** Review spelling, grammar, and typography suggestions in the bottom panel, jump directly to line/column, or add terms to your ignore list."},"99":{"id":"/docs/getting-started","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting Started","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started"},"100":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"First-time launch, workspace panes, file management, and compiling your first Typst document."},"101":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"Workspace Layout"},"102":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#creating-and-opening-projects","content":"Creating and Opening Projects"},"103":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"Writing and Compiling Typst"},"104":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"When you launch **azo-type** without a directory argument, it opens an **in-memory blank project** so you can start typing Typst markup immediately without creating files up front."},"105":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"The IDE is organized into four main areas:"},"106":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Menu Bar (`File`, `Edit`, `View`, `Project`)**:"},"107":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"On **Linux** and **Windows**, an in-window menu bar sits across the top, including a quick **Panel** toggle and active folder indicator."},"108":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"On **macOS**, `azo-type` installs a native screen-top menu bar via `muda`."},"109":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Left Sidebar (`Ctrl+B` / `Cmd+B`)**:"},"110":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Disk Project Tree:** Browse directories and files with type badges (`[T]` Typst, `[B]` BibTeX/YAML, `[S]` SVG, `[I]` images, `[F]` text, `[#]` binary), dirty indicators (`*`), main-file star (`★`), and live P2P peer presence markers."},"111":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Document Outline:** Hierarchical AST heading tree showing section numbers and line locations."},"112":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Center Code Editor & Preview Split**:"},"113":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Tabbed Typst Editor:** Line-number gutter, active line highlighting, syntax coloring, formatting toolbar, and asset inspector for images/SVGs."},"114":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Live Document Preview:** Resizable split divider (drag to resize, double-click to reset 50/50) displaying compiled pages in real time."},"115":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Bottom Workspace Panel (`Ctrl+J` / `Cmd+J`)**:"},"116":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Warnings & Errors:** Clickable compiler diagnostics with `file:line:col` jump links and compiler hints."},"117":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Console:** Recorded runtime and tool output."},"118":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#workspace-layout","content":"**Language Auto-Correction:** Offline spelling, grammar, and typography check results."},"119":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#creating-and-opening-projects","content":"**Open Folder (`Ctrl+O` / `Cmd+O`):** Choose an existing Typst project directory via the native OS folder picker. Internal directories such as `target/`, `node_modules/`, and `shots/` are skipped during tree scans."},"120":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#creating-and-opening-projects","content":"**Create a New File (`Ctrl+N` / `Cmd+N`):** Use **+ File** in the sidebar or the File menu to create nested paths (e.g., `chapters/results.typ`). New `.typ` files are seeded with a default heading template."},"121":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#creating-and-opening-projects","content":"**Set Main Entrypoint:** Right-click any `.typ` file in the sidebar (or select **Project → Set Active File as Main Entrypoint**) to designate the root document compiled into the preview and PDF export."},"122":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#creating-and-opening-projects","content":"**Save Work (`Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S`):** If you started in an in-memory blank document, pressing Save prompts you to pick a destination on disk. With **Auto-save modified files to disk as you type** enabled (on by default for disk projects), edits flush automatically."},"123":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"Use the editor formatting toolbar or right-click context menu to insert common Typst constructs quickly:"},"124":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-24","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"**`= Heading`** — Inserts a new section (`== New Section`)."},"125":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-25","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"**`*Bold*`** / **`_Italic_`** — Wraps the current selection or inserts formatted placeholders."},"126":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-26","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"**`$ Math $`** — Inserts a display math equation block."},"127":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-27","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"**`+ Table`** — Inserts a two-column `#table(...)` block."},"128":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-28","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"**`+ Figure`** — Inserts a `#figure(image(...))` template."},"129":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-29","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#writing-and-compiling-typst","content":"As you type, `azo-type` debounces compilation (default `120 ms`) on a background thread and updates the status bar with compilation timing, page count, and active Typst compiler version. External `@preview/...` packages referenced in your document are downloaded automatically via `typst-kit`."},"130":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"131":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Overview of azo-type, a native cross-platform Rust desktop editor for Typst with live preview and P2P collaboration."},"132":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-azo-type","content":"Why azo-type?"},"133":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"Architecture at a Glance"},"134":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"Next Steps"},"135":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**azo-type** (Azo Type) is a native, local-first desktop editor for authoring Typst documents. Built in Rust with `egui`/`eframe`, it combines incremental Typst compilation, AST-driven outline navigation, standards-compliant PDF export, offline spell and grammar checking, and zero-server peer-to-peer collaboration."},"136":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"azo-type is currently in early pre-alpha development. Features and interfaces are actively evolving—please report bugs or feedback on the GitHub repository."},"137":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-azo-type","content":"**Local-First Native Speed:** Written in Rust (`2021` edition) with an immediate-mode `egui` / `eframe` `0.31` GPU-accelerated interface (`glow`)."},"138":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-azo-type","content":"**Bundled Typst Runtime:** Ships with Typst `0.15.1` and 17 embedded fonts out of the box, plus optional SHA-256 verified downloads of legacy Typst versions (`0.14.2`, `0.13.1`, `0.12.0`)."},"139":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-azo-type","content":"**Zero-Server P2P Collaboration:** Powered by `yrs` (`0.28`, Yjs CRDT) over direct `iroh` (`1.4.1`) QUIC streams—no central accounts or cloud servers required."},"140":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-azo-type","content":"**Archival & Accessible PDF Export:** Supports PDF `1.4`–`2.0`, ISO 19005 PDF/A standards (`1a`/`1b` through `4`/`4f`/`4e`), PDF/UA-1, and tagged document structure trees."},"141":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-azo-type","content":"**Offline Proofreading:** Optional offline spellchecking (`spellbook`), grammar rules (`nlprule`), and automatic language detection (`lingua`)."},"142":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"The desktop application in `/app` follows strict inward dependency inversion so pure domain logic stays independent of GUI and network frameworks:"},"143":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"| Layer               | Modules (`app/src/`)                                     | Responsibility                                                                            |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **UI Presentation** | `app.rs`, `ui/components/`, `ui/dialogs/`, `ui/theme.rs` | Immediate-mode panels, editor canvas, preview pane, modal sub-windows, and design tokens. |","table":"table-0"},"144":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"| Layer                    | Modules (`app/src/`)                                                                        | Responsibility                                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Application Services** | `compiler.rs`, `world.rs`, `collab/`, `engine/`, `language_check/`, `project/`, `services/` | Background Typst compilation, P2P actor runtime, workspace buffers, and language packs. |","table":"table-0"},"145":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"| Layer                    | Modules (`app/src/`)                                                                   | Responsibility                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Platform Abstraction** | `platform/menu.rs`, `platform/dialogs.rs`, `platform/shortcuts.rs`, `platform/icon.rs` | macOS `muda` menu bar, async `rfd` file pickers, global hotkeys, and desktop integration. |","table":"table-0"},"146":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"| Layer           | Modules (`app/src/`)                                                                                       | Responsibility                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Core Domain** | `core/outline.rs`, `core/diff.rs`, `core/pdf.rs`, `core/settings.rs`, `core/spellcheck.rs`, `core/i18n.rs` | Pure Rust AST outline parsing, UTF-16 CRDT diffing, PDF validation, settings schema, and localization. |","table":"table-0"},"147":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Installation\" description=\"Install azo-type on Linux, macOS, or Windows, or build from source with Cargo.\" href=\"/docs/installation\" />"},"148":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Getting Started\" description=\"Learn the workspace layout, file tree, editor tools, and live preview.\" href=\"/docs/getting-started\" />"},"149":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Features\" description=\"Explore P2P collaboration, PDF/A export, AST outline, and spell/grammar checking.\" href=\"/docs/features\" />"},"150":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Configuration\" description=\"Customize themes, compiler settings, keyboard shortcuts, and UI language.\" href=\"/docs/configuration\" />"},"151":{"id":"/docs/installation","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation"},"152":{"id":"/docs/installation-0","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation","content":"Install azo-type on Linux, macOS, and Windows, or compile from source using Rust and Cargo."},"153":{"id":"/docs/installation-1","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#release-binaries","content":"Release Binaries"},"154":{"id":"/docs/installation-2","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#building-from-source","content":"Building from Source"},"155":{"id":"/docs/installation-3","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"156":{"id":"/docs/installation-4","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#compile-and-run","content":"Compile and Run"},"157":{"id":"/docs/installation-5","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#command-line-options","content":"Command-Line Options"},"158":{"id":"/docs/installation-6","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation","content":"azo-type targets **Linux** (Wayland & X11), **macOS** (Apple Silicon `aarch64` & Intel `x86_64`), and **Windows** (`x86_64` & `aarch64`)."},"159":{"id":"/docs/installation-7","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#release-binaries","content":"Pre-built release archives are published on GitHub Releases (and directly on the Download page)."},"160":{"id":"/docs/installation-8","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#release-binaries","content":"Download the archive or installer matching your operating system and CPU architecture."},"161":{"id":"/docs/installation-9","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#release-binaries","content":"Extract or install the `azo-type` executable (`azo-type.exe` on Windows, `Azo Type.app` on macOS)."},"162":{"id":"/docs/installation-10","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#release-binaries","content":"Launch the binary directly—Typst `0.15.1` and 17 bundled fonts are embedded inside the application, so no external `typst` CLI installation is required."},"163":{"id":"/docs/installation-11","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#release-binaries","content":"azo-type is currently in early pre-alpha development, and pre-built release binaries are not yet ready to download. Building from source with Cargo below is currently the recommended way to run the application."},"164":{"id":"/docs/installation-12","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#prerequisites","content":"**Rust `1.80+`** (stable toolchain via rustup)"},"165":{"id":"/docs/installation-13","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#prerequisites","content":"**C compiler toolchain** (`gcc`/`clang` on Linux, Xcode Command Line Tools on macOS, MSVC Build Tools on Windows)"},"166":{"id":"/docs/installation-14","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#prerequisites","content":"**Linux system libraries:** `fontconfig` development headers plus X11/Wayland libraries"},"167":{"id":"/docs/installation-15","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#prerequisites","content":"On Debian/Ubuntu Linux, install the required development packages before compiling:"},"168":{"id":"/docs/installation-16","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#compile-and-run","content":"Clone the repository and build the desktop application from `/app`:"},"169":{"id":"/docs/installation-17","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#compile-and-run","content":"The release profile in `app/Cargo.toml` uses `opt-level = 3`, `lto = \"fat\"`, `codegen-units = 1`, and `strip = true`. The resulting binary is written to `app/target/release/azo-type` (or `azo-type.exe` on Windows)."},"170":{"id":"/docs/installation-18","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#command-line-options","content":"`azo-type` accepts optional CLI arguments at startup (parsed in `app/src/lib.rs`):"},"171":{"id":"/docs/installation-19","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#command-line-options","content":"| Invocation | Behavior                                                                         |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type` | Starts directly in an in-memory blank Typst project ready for immediate editing. |","table":"table-0"},"172":{"id":"/docs/installation-20","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#command-line-options","content":"| Invocation          | Behavior                                                    |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type <folder>` | Opens the specified project directory if it exists on disk. |","table":"table-0"},"173":{"id":"/docs/installation-21","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#command-line-options","content":"| Invocation                     | Behavior                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type --screenshot <path>` | Headless CI capture mode: renders the UI, writes a PNG/JPEG screenshot to `<path>`, and exits. |","table":"table-0"},"174":{"id":"/docs/installation-22","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation#command-line-options","content":"| Invocation                     | Behavior                                           |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type --screenshot=<path>` | Equivalent equals-sign form for screenshot output. |","table":"table-0"}},"count":174},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":114,"2":152,"3":155,"4":97,"5":98,"6":99,"7":100,"8":134,"9":137,"10":146,"11":34,"12":17,"13":27,"14":63,"15":37,"16":54,"17":10,"18":53,"19":6,"20":60,"21":9,"22":58,"23":48,"24":47,"25":28,"26":8,"27":29,"28":25,"29":22,"30":144,"31":82,"32":83,"33":86,"34":88,"35":87,"36":85,"37":84,"38":80,"39":78,"40":79,"41":81,"42":164,"43":115,"44":109,"45":154,"46":169,"47":133,"48":170,"49":116,"50":108,"51":66,"52":71,"53":70,"54":73,"55":72,"56":162,"57":67,"58":121,"59":117,"60":159,"61":122,"62":126,"63":119,"64":136,"65":138,"66":129,"67":173,"68":156,"69":140,"70":69,"71":49,"72":65,"73":16,"74":30,"75":167,"76":59,"77":36,"78":160,"79":125,"80":151,"81":101,"82":104,"83":145,"84":20,"85":23,"86":32,"87":46,"88":163,"89":150,"90":44,"91":45,"92":5,"93":18,"94":120,"95":61,"96":56,"97":57,"98":31,"99":128,"100":127,"101":171,"102":118,"103":172,"104":166,"105":158,"106":41,"107":141,"108":142,"109":35,"110":24,"111":26,"112":15,"113":55,"114":39,"115":12,"116":62,"117":19,"118":33,"119":43,"120":21,"121":52,"122":51,"123":165,"124":3,"125":0,"126":4,"127":2,"128":1,"129":103,"130":132,"131":147,"132":168,"133":102,"134":139,"135":11,"136":106,"137":40,"138":13,"139":64,"140":7,"141":42,"142":157,"143":95,"144":93,"145":94,"146":96,"147":77,"148":76,"149":75,"150":74,"151":131,"152":130,"153":153,"154":110,"155":149,"156":113,"157":112,"158":107,"159":148,"160":123,"161":124,"162":135,"163":105,"164":50,"165":14,"166":38,"167":143,"168":111,"169":161,"170":68,"171":92,"172":91,"173":89,"174":90},"orderedDocs":[[125,"**`*Bold*`** / **`_Italic_`** — Wraps the current selection or inserts formatted placeholders."],[128,"**`+ Figure`** — Inserts a `#figure(image(...))` template."],[127,"**`+ Table`** — Inserts a two-column `#table(...)` block."],[124,"**`= Heading`** — Inserts a new section (`== New Section`)."],[126,"**`$ Math $`** — Inserts a display math equation block."],[92,"**Accessibility:** Toggle **PDF/UA-1** (ISO 14289-1) and **Tagged PDF** structure tree generation."],[19,"**Active Project Folder:** Inspect the active workspace root, switch folders, or trigger a disk rescan."],[140,"**Archival & Accessible PDF Export:** Supports PDF `1.4`–`2.0`, ISO 19005 PDF/A standards (`1a`/`1b` through `4`/`4f`/`4e`), PDF/UA-1, and tagged document structure trees."],[26,"**Auto-Check While Typing:** Debounced background checking (`150 ms`–`2000 ms`, default `450 ms`)."],[21,"**Auto-Compile on Type:** Incrementally recompile while editing (enabled by default)."],[17,"**Auto-Save on Edit:** Automatically write modified disk buffers as you type (enabled by default)."],[135,"**azo-type** (Azo Type) is a native, local-first desktop editor for authoring Typst documents. Built in Rust with `egui`/`eframe`, it combines incremental Typst compilation, AST-driven outline navigation, standards-compliant PDF export, offline spell and grammar checking, and zero-server peer-to-peer collaboration."],[115,"**Bottom Workspace Panel (`Ctrl+J` / `Cmd+J`)**:"],[138,"**Bundled Typst Runtime:** Ships with Typst `0.15.1` and 17 embedded fonts out of the box, plus optional SHA-256 verified downloads of legacy Typst versions (`0.14.2`, `0.13.1`, `0.12.0`)."],[165,"**C compiler toolchain** (`gcc`/`clang` on Linux, Xcode Command Line Tools on macOS, MSVC Build Tools on Windows)"],[112,"**Center Code Editor & Preview Split**:"],[73,"**Click & Drag Text Selection:** Select text directly on rendered preview pages to copy it or automatically jump the editor cursor back to the corresponding Typst source range (**Auto-Jump**)."],[12,"**Color Theme:** Choose **Dark** (`#1C1B22`), **Light** (`#FFFFFF`), or **System-Default** (tracks OS dark/light preference)."],[93,"**Compatibility Guard:** Automatically validates combinations (for example, `PDF/A-1` requires `PDF 1.4` and `PDF/A-4` requires `PDF 2.0`), offers a one-click compatible version switch, and displays the equivalent `typst compile --pdf-standard` CLI flags."],[117,"**Console:** Recorded runtime and tool output."],[84,"**CRDT Synchronization (`yrs`):** Multi-file project state is synced via Yjs CRDT updates (`Origin::from(\"local\")` vs `Origin::from(\"remote\")`), preserving cursor positions with `StickyIndex` and isolating each peer's undo/redo history (`yrs::UndoManager`)."],[120,"**Create a New File (`Ctrl+N` / `Cmd+N`):** Use **+ File** in the sidebar or the File menu to create nested paths (e.g., `chapters/results.typ`). New `.typ` files are seeded with a default heading template."],[29,"**Dictionaries:** Download/remove Tier-1 language packs, import Tier-2 `.dic`/`.aff` files, and manage ignored words."],[85,"**Direct QUIC Transport (`iroh`):** Hosts bind an `iroh` QUIC endpoint (`b\"azo-type/collab/v1\"`) and generate a 256-bit secret invite ticket prefixed with `typst-collab-v1:`."],[110,"**Disk Project Tree:** Browse directories and files with type badges (`[T]` Typst, `[B]` BibTeX/YAML, `[S]` SVG, `[I]` images, `[F]` text, `[#]` binary), dirty indicators (`*`), main-file star (`★`), and live P2P peer presence markers."],[28,"**Document Language Override:** `Auto` (reads `#set text(lang: ...)` or runs Lingua detection) or explicit `en` / `de` / `fr` / `es`."],[111,"**Document Outline:** Hierarchical AST heading tree showing section numbers and line locations."],[13,"**Editor Font Size:** Adjustable from `10.0 pt` to `22.0 pt` (default `13.5 pt`)."],[25,"**Enable Spell & Grammar Checking:** Master toggle (disabled by default)."],[27,"**Grammar & Typography Rules:** Toggle `nlprule` and pure-Rust typography/repetition checks."],[74,"**Hand Pan Mode:** Switch to **Hand Pan** in the preview toolbar to drag-pan across zoomed pages without triggering text selection."],[98,"**Interactive Diagnostics:** Review spelling, grammar, and typography suggestions in the bottom panel, jump directly to line/column, or add terms to your ignore list."],[86,"**LAN / Localhost Only Mode:** Optionally disable public relays when collaborating on a trusted local network."],[118,"**Language Auto-Correction:** Offline spelling, grammar, and typography check results."],[11,"**Language:** Switch UI language at runtime (`English` or `Deutsch`), or follow the OS locale detected at startup via `sys-locale`."],[109,"**Left Sidebar (`Ctrl+B` / `Cmd+B`)**:"],[77,"**Legacy Typst `0.14.2`, `0.13.1`, and `0.12.0`** (downloaded on demand from official Typst GitHub releases for your host triple and verified against embedded SHA-256 checksums before activation)"],[15,"**Line Numbers Gutter:** Show or hide line numbers beside the editor."],[166,"**Linux system libraries:** `fontconfig` development headers plus X11/Wayland libraries"],[114,"**Live Document Preview:** Resizable split divider (drag to resize, double-click to reset 50/50) displaying compiled pages in real time."],[137,"**Local-First Native Speed:** Written in Rust (`2021` edition) with an immediate-mode `egui` / `eframe` `0.31` GPU-accelerated interface (`glow`)."],[106,"**Menu Bar (`File`, `Edit`, `View`, `Project`)**:"],[141,"**Offline Proofreading:** Optional offline spellchecking (`spellbook`), grammar rules (`nlprule`), and automatic language detection (`lingua`)."],[119,"**Open Folder (`Ctrl+O` / `Cmd+O`):** Choose an existing Typst project directory via the native OS folder picker. Internal directories such as `target/`, `node_modules/`, and `shots/` are skipped during tree scans."],[90,"**PDF Versions:** `1.4`, `1.5`, `1.6`, `1.7` (default), and `2.0`."],[91,"**PDF/A Archival Standards (ISO 19005):** `PDF/A-1b`, `PDF/A-1a`, `PDF/A-2b`, `PDF/A-2u`, `PDF/A-2a`, `PDF/A-3b`, `PDF/A-3u`, `PDF/A-3a`, `PDF/A-4`, `PDF/A-4f`, and `PDF/A-4e`."],[87,"**Peer Presence & Persistence:** Displays connected peers with custom display names, cursor colors, active file indicators, and connection routes (`Direct` vs `Relay` with RTT). Snapshots are saved to `.typst-collab/` with path-traversal protection and deterministic conflict naming (`<stem>.conflict-<id>.<ext>`)."],[24,"**Preview Interaction:** Toggle **Auto-Jump** source selection sync and **Hand Pan** mode."],[23,"**Preview Rasterization Scale:** `1.5x Fast`, `2.0x Crisp` (default), or `3.0x Ultra HiDPI`."],[71,"**Rasterization DPI:** Choose between **1.5x Fast**, **2.0x Crisp** (default), and **3.0x Ultra HiDPI** in Settings."],[164,"**Rust `1.80+`** (stable toolchain via rustup)"],[122,"**Save Work (`Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S`):** If you started in an in-memory blank document, pressing Save prompts you to pick a destination on disk. With **Auto-save modified files to disk as you type** enabled (on by default for disk projects), edits flush automatically."],[121,"**Set Main Entrypoint:** Right-click any `.typ` file in the sidebar (or select **Project → Set Active File as Main Entrypoint**) to designate the root document compiled into the preview and PDF export."],[18,"**Show Hidden Files:** Display dotfiles and hidden directories (such as `.git` or `.vscode`) in the sidebar file tree."],[16,"**Syntax Highlighting:** Toggle real-time Typst syntax highlighting powered by `typst-syntax`."],[113,"**Tabbed Typst Editor:** Line-number gutter, active line highlighting, syntax coloring, formatting toolbar, and asset inspector for images/SVGs."],[96,"**Tier-1 Language Packs (`en`, `de`, `fr`, `es`):** Download Hunspell dictionaries (`spellbook`) and `nlprule` grammar binaries on demand with SHA-256 verification. Language detection (`lingua`) or `#set text(lang: \"...\")` automatically selects the active language when set to `Auto`."],[97,"**Tier-2 Custom Hunspell Dictionaries:** Import any local `.dic` / `.aff` dictionary pair from disk (automatically transcoded to UTF-8)."],[22,"**Typing Debounce Interval:** Configurable from `50 ms` to `800 ms` (default `120 ms`)."],[76,"**Typst `0.15.1`** (built-in offline default)"],[20,"**Typst Compiler Version:** Use built-in `0.15.1` or download/activate legacy `0.14.2`, `0.13.1`, or `0.12.0` releases."],[95,"**Typst-Aware Prose Extraction:** Masks code, math, labels, comments, and syntax tokens before checking prose."],[116,"**Warnings & Errors:** Clickable compiler diagnostics with `file:line:col` jump links and compiler hints."],[14,"**Word Wrap:** Automatically wrap long lines to the editor pane width with `↩` continuation markers."],[139,"**Zero-Server P2P Collaboration:** Powered by `yrs` (`0.28`, Yjs CRDT) over direct `iroh` (`1.4.1`) QUIC streams—no central accounts or cloud servers required."],[72,"**Zoom & Navigation:** Toggle **Fit Width**, select preset zoom percentages (`50%`–`200%`), or hold `Ctrl` + mouse wheel over the preview (`25%`–`400%`)."],[51,"`./scripts/check.sh` enforces four checks:"],[57,"`app/src/core/` must remain pure Rust with **zero** GUI (`egui`/`eframe`), OS dialog (`rfd`/`muda`), or async/P2P (`tokio`/`iroh`) imports."],[170,"`azo-type` accepts optional CLI arguments at startup (parsed in `app/src/lib.rs`):"],[70,"`azo-type` renders compiled Typst pages to RGBA textures using `typst_render` on a non-blocking worker thread:"],[53,"`cargo clippy --all-targets --manifest-path app/Cargo.toml -- -D warnings`"],[52,"`cargo fmt --check --manifest-path app/Cargo.toml`"],[55,"`cargo test --manifest-path app/Cargo.toml` (unit tests, integration tests, and headless `egui_kittest` UI tests)"],[54,"`python3 scripts/verify_structural_rules.py` (enforces inward layer boundaries, `//!` module docs, file size limits, externalized tests in `app/src/tests/`, and `docs/agent/PROJECT_MAP.md` synchronization)"],[150,"<Card title=\"Configuration\" description=\"Customize themes, compiler settings, keyboard shortcuts, and UI language.\" href=\"/docs/configuration\" />"],[149,"<Card title=\"Features\" description=\"Explore P2P collaboration, PDF/A export, AST outline, and spell/grammar checking.\" href=\"/docs/features\" />"],[148,"<Card title=\"Getting Started\" description=\"Learn the workspace layout, file tree, editor tools, and live preview.\" href=\"/docs/getting-started\" />"],[147,"<Card title=\"Installation\" description=\"Install azo-type on Linux, macOS, or Windows, or build from source with Cargo.\" href=\"/docs/installation\" />"],[39,"| Action                          | Windows / Linux                               | macOS                         |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Undo / Redo (incl. CRDT Collab) | `Ctrl + Z` / `Ctrl + Y` or `Ctrl + Shift + Z` | `Cmd + Z` / `Cmd + Shift + Z` |"],[40,"| Action                          | Windows / Linux              | macOS                       |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Cut / Copy / Paste / Select All | `Ctrl + X` / `C` / `V` / `A` | `Cmd + X` / `C` / `V` / `A` |"],[38,"| Action                | Windows / Linux | macOS |\n| --------------------- | --------------- | ----- |\n| Rescan Folder on Disk | `F5`            | `F5`  |"],[41,"| Action              | Windows / Linux      | macOS               |\n| ------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Zoom Preview Canvas | `Ctrl + Mouse Wheel` | `Cmd + Mouse Wheel` |"],[31,"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| New File in Project | `Ctrl + N`      | `Cmd + N` |"],[32,"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Open Project Folder | `Ctrl + O`      | `Cmd + O` |"],[37,"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Toggle Bottom Panel | `Ctrl + J`      | `Cmd + J` |"],[36,"| Action              | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Toggle Left Sidebar | `Ctrl + B`      | `Cmd + B` |"],[33,"| Action           | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Save Active File | `Ctrl + S`      | `Cmd + S` |"],[35,"| Action        | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Open Settings | `Ctrl + ,`      | `Cmd + ,` |"],[34,"| Action     | Windows / Linux | macOS     |\n| ---------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Export PDF | `Ctrl + E`      | `Cmd + E` |"],[173,"| Invocation                     | Behavior                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type --screenshot <path>` | Headless CI capture mode: renders the UI, writes a PNG/JPEG screenshot to `<path>`, and exits. |"],[174,"| Invocation                     | Behavior                                           |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type --screenshot=<path>` | Equivalent equals-sign form for screenshot output. |"],[172,"| Invocation          | Behavior                                                    |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type <folder>` | Opens the specified project directory if it exists on disk. |"],[171,"| Invocation | Behavior                                                                         |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `azo-type` | Starts directly in an in-memory blank Typst project ready for immediate editing. |"],[144,"| Layer                    | Modules (`app/src/`)                                                                        | Responsibility                                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Application Services** | `compiler.rs`, `world.rs`, `collab/`, `engine/`, `language_check/`, `project/`, `services/` | Background Typst compilation, P2P actor runtime, workspace buffers, and language packs. |"],[145,"| Layer                    | Modules (`app/src/`)                                                                   | Responsibility                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Platform Abstraction** | `platform/menu.rs`, `platform/dialogs.rs`, `platform/shortcuts.rs`, `platform/icon.rs` | macOS `muda` menu bar, async `rfd` file pickers, global hotkeys, and desktop integration. |"],[143,"| Layer               | Modules (`app/src/`)                                     | Responsibility                                                                            |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **UI Presentation** | `app.rs`, `ui/components/`, `ui/dialogs/`, `ui/theme.rs` | Immediate-mode panels, editor canvas, preview pane, modal sub-windows, and design tokens. |"],[146,"| Layer           | Modules (`app/src/`)                                                                                       | Responsibility                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Core Domain** | `core/outline.rs`, `core/diff.rs`, `core/pdf.rs`, `core/settings.rs`, `core/spellcheck.rs`, `core/i18n.rs` | Pure Rust AST outline parsing, UTF-16 CRDT diffing, PDF validation, settings schema, and localization. |"],[4,"1. Appearance"],[5,"2. Editor & Filesystem"],[6,"3. Compiler & Preview"],[7,"4. Spell & Grammar"],[81,"Also parses Markdown `# Heading` sections and BibTeX `@article{key, ...}` citation entries."],[133,"Architecture at a Glance"],[129,"As you type, `azo-type` debounces compilation (default `120 ms`) on a background thread and updates the status bar with compilation timing, page count, and active Typst compiler version. External `@preview/...` packages referenced in your document are downloaded automatically via `typst-kit`."],[82,"Assigns hierarchical numbering (`1`, `1.1`, `1.1.1`) and highlights the heading matching your current cursor position."],[163,"azo-type is currently in early pre-alpha development, and pre-built release binaries are not yet ready to download. Building from source with Cargo below is currently the recommended way to run the application."],[136,"azo-type is currently in early pre-alpha development. Features and interfaces are actively evolving—please report bugs or feedback on the GitHub repository."],[158,"azo-type targets **Linux** (Wayland & X11), **macOS** (Apple Silicon `aarch64` & Intel `x86_64`), and **Windows** (`x86_64` & `aarch64`)."],[50,"Before submitting any pull request touching Rust code, run the unified quality gate from the repository root:"],[44,"Build, test, lint, and contribute to the azo-type desktop app (/app) and documentation website (/website)."],[154,"Building from Source"],[168,"Clone the repository and build the desktop application from `/app`:"],[157,"Command-Line Options"],[156,"Compile and Run"],[1,"Configuration & Shortcuts"],[43,"Contributing"],[49,"Contributions to **azo-type** are welcome across both the Rust desktop IDE (`/app`) and this documentation site (`/website`). All code in this repository is licensed under the **GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)**."],[59,"Create commits on a dedicated branch using Conventional Commits (`feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `docs(...)`, `refactor(...)`, `test(...)`)."],[102,"Creating and Opening Projects"],[63,"Deep dive into azo-type capabilities—live preview, Typst version switching, AST outline, P2P collaboration, PDF/A export, and offline proofreading."],[94,"Disabled by default so it stays out of your way until needed, offline proofreading runs strictly locally inside **azo-type**:"],[58,"Do not place inline `mod tests { ... }` blocks inside production `.rs` files—wire unit tests via `#[cfg(test)] #[path = \"...\"] mod tests;` into `app/src/tests/`."],[61,"Documentation pages live in `website/content/docs/*.mdx`, ordered by `website/content/docs/meta.json`."],[160,"Download the archive or installer matching your operating system and CPU architecture."],[161,"Extract or install the `azo-type` executable (`azo-type.exe` on Windows, `Azo Type.app` on macOS)."],[79,"Extracts `= ...` markup headings and `#heading(level: ...)[...]` calls while ignoring headings inside comments, raw code blocks, and `show heading.where(...)` styling rules."],[62,"Features"],[100,"First-time launch, workspace panes, file management, and compiling your first Typst document."],[99,"Getting Started"],[66,"Hierarchical AST Document Outline"],[152,"Install azo-type on Linux, macOS, and Windows, or compile from source using Rust and Cargo."],[151,"Installation"],[130,"Introduction"],[47,"Key Architectural Rules"],[8,"Keyboard Shortcuts"],[162,"Launch the binary directly—Typst `0.15.1` and 17 bundled fonts are embedded inside the application, so no external `typst` CLI installation is required."],[64,"Live Preview & Interactive Source Sync"],[9,"Localization"],[65,"Multi-Version Typst Compiler Engine"],[134,"Next Steps"],[69,"Offline Spell & Grammar Checking"],[107,"On **Linux** and **Windows**, an in-window menu bar sits across the top, including a quick **Panel** toggle and active folder indicator."],[108,"On **macOS**, `azo-type` installs a native screen-top menu bar via `muda`."],[167,"On Debian/Ubuntu Linux, install the required development packages before compiling:"],[30,"On macOS, `Ctrl` corresponds to `Cmd` (`Modifiers::COMMAND` in `app/src/platform/shortcuts.rs`):"],[83,"Open **Project → Collaboration (P2P)...** to co-author an entire project folder in real time without central servers:"],[10,"Open the **Settings** sub-window via **File → Settings...** or `Ctrl+,` (`Cmd+,` on macOS). Preferences are persisted across restarts via `eframe` storage (`app/src/core/settings.rs`)."],[131,"Overview of azo-type, a native cross-platform Rust desktop editor for Typst with live preview and P2P collaboration."],[159,"Pre-built release archives are published on GitHub Releases (and directly on the Download page)."],[155,"Prerequisites"],[89,"Press `Ctrl+E` (`Cmd+E` on macOS) or choose **File → Export PDF...** to configure standards-checked PDF output:"],[80,"Recursively resolves `#include \"...\"` and `#module` imports across project files and merges compiled outline items from templates."],[2,"Reference for azo-type Settings tabs, keyboard shortcuts, design tokens, and UI localization."],[153,"Release Binaries"],[45,"Repository Structure"],[3,"Settings Tabs"],[68,"Standards-Compliant PDF Export"],[142,"The desktop application in `/app` follows strict inward dependency inversion so pure domain logic stays independent of GUI and network frameworks:"],[105,"The IDE is organized into four main areas:"],[60,"The marketing pages and documentation are built with Next.js static export (`output: 'export'`) and Fumadocs."],[78,"The outline parser (`app/src/core/outline.rs`) inspects the Typst AST (`typst-syntax`) rather than naive regexes:"],[169,"The release profile in `app/Cargo.toml` uses `opt-level = 3`, `lto = \"fat\"`, `codegen-units = 1`, and `strip = true`. The resulting binary is written to `app/target/release/azo-type` (or `azo-type.exe` on Windows)."],[56,"To inspect line coverage with `cargo-llvm-cov`:"],[88,"Treat `typst-collab-v1:` invite tickets like passwords—anyone holding a ticket can join the active P2P session. Use the **Mask Ticket** toggle when screen-sharing."],[42,"UI strings live in monolingual Weblate-compatible YAML files under `locales/` (`locales/en.yml`, `locales/de.yml`) powered by `rust-i18n`. New translations can be added by creating a matching `locales/<lang>.yml` file and registering it in `app/src/core/i18n.rs`."],[123,"Use the editor formatting toolbar or right-click context menu to insert common Typst constructs quickly:"],[104,"When you launch **azo-type** without a directory argument, it opens an **in-memory blank project** so you can start typing Typst markup immediately without creating files up front."],[75,"While Typst `0.15.1` is compiled directly into `azo-type`, older documents may target earlier Typst releases. In **Settings → Compiler & Preview** (or by clicking the Typst version badge in the status bar), you can switch between:"],[132,"Why azo-type?"],[46,"Working on the Desktop App (`/app`)"],[48,"Working on the Website (`/website`)"],[101,"Workspace Layout"],[103,"Writing and Compiling Typst"],[67,"Zero-Server P2P Collaboration"]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":21,"2":22,"3":23,"4":24,"5":25,"6":26,"7":27,"8":28,"9":29,"10":30,"11":31,"12":32,"13":33,"14":34,"15":35,"16":36,"17":37,"18":38,"19":39,"20":40,"21":41,"22":42,"23":43,"24":44,"25":45,"26":46,"27":47,"28":48,"29":49,"30":50,"31":51,"32":52,"33":53,"34":54,"35":55,"36":56,"37":57,"38":58,"39":59,"40":60,"41":61,"42":62,"43":63,"44":64,"45":65,"46":66,"47":67,"48":68,"49":